=== 2. Segmentation / phase head redundancy ===
  Dice(seg head, threshold(predicted phase)) measures how much of the
  segmentation output is already implied by the reconstruction.

  modality       head vs GT   derived vs GT   head vs derived
  off_axis           0.8221          0.8283            0.9203
  gabor              0.7509          0.7466            0.9115

  -> the two heads are largely redundant. Thresholding the predicted
     phase reproduces the segmentation head, which is the expected
     consequence of deriving the masks from the phase and is the
     mechanism behind the null result for the physics-consistency
     terms: those terms constrain a quantity already determined by
     the two primary losses. State this in the paper.

